IMPORT prelude

-- Code of Alabama 1975, Title 25, Chapter 4 (Unemployment Compensation) -- what an unemployed worker can get.
--
-- Edition: the text ALISON served on 2026-10-20, as deposited at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ala-code-25-4-art4.txt (Article 4, Benefits, ss 25-4-70 to 25-4-78)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ala-code-25-4-art5.txt (Article 5, Claims procedure, ss 25-4-90 to 25-4-97)
-- ALISON publishes no 'current through' date.
--
-- In: s 25-4-72(b), (b)(1), (2), (5) (the weekly benefit amount, for benefit years beginning on or after 1 January 2020);
-- s 25-4-73(a), (c) (the weekly payment; partial earnings; the waiting week); s 25-4-74(a) (the maximum total in a benefit
-- year); s 25-4-77(a)(1)-(6) (weekly eligibility, the work search, the base-period wage test and requalification);
-- s 25-4-78(2) (voluntary quit), (3) (discharge for misconduct), (5) (refusing suitable work), (8) (employer pensions);
-- s 25-4-91(d)(1) (the time to appeal; repaying disputed benefits).
--
-- Out: benefit years beginning before 1 January 2020 (`not covered`); maritime workers (s 25-4-76); extended benefits
-- (s 25-4-75; federal frame in subjects/us/federal-state-extended-unemployment-compensation-act-of-1970); the training
-- extension of s 25-4-74(f); s 25-4-78(1), (4), (6), (7), (9)-(13) and the rest of s 25-4-78; employer charging (s 25-4-54);
-- who is an employer and what is insured work (Article 1): the worker states wages for insured work.
--
-- Federal frame (not imported): FUTA 26 U.S.C. 3304 and SSA Title III, deposited in subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986
-- and subjects/us/social-security-act. Unemployment compensation is federal gross income (26 U.S.C. 85); Alabama exempts
-- some after a downsizing (s 40-18-19.1, encoded in ../../../code-of-alabama-1975-title-40-chapter-18-income-taxes/).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, from the seat of the unemployed worker (the claimant). Expected values in the case file are
-- hand-written. No pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT ADVICE.

§ `Code of Alabama 1975, Title 25, Chapter 4 -- unemployment compensation benefits`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 25-4-72(a), (b)(3), (4): benefit years before 2020 had other maximums (and before 2006 another formula)
    `this encoding computes benefits for benefit years beginning on or after 1 January 2020 only`

DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- s 25-4-72(1), s 25-4-73(a), s 25-4-74(a): "fractional parts of one dollar ($1) in excess of fifty cents ($.50) shall be
-- rounded to the next higher multiple ... fractional parts ... which are fifty cents ($.50) or less shall be dropped". The
-- same rule is used for "computed to the nearest multiple of one dollar" in ss 25-4-73 and 25-4-74 (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the dollar` MEANS
    IF (`amount` MINUS FLOOR `amount`) GREATER THAN 0.5
    THEN FLOOR `amount` PLUS 1
    ELSE FLOOR `amount`

§§ `s 25-4-72 -- the weekly benefit amount`

-- (b): "one twenty-sixth of the average of the wages for insured work paid to the individual during the two quarters of
-- his or her base period in which the total wages were the highest"; (2): if that is not more than $44.50 "there shall be
-- no weekly benefit amount"; (5): from benefit years beginning on or after 1 January 2020, above $274.50 the maximum is
-- $275. Wages in the two highest quarters are stated by the worker.
GIVEN `wages in the highest quarter` IS A NUMBER, `wages in the second-highest quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount derived` MEANS
    ((`wages in the highest quarter` PLUS `wages in the second-highest quarter`) DIVIDED BY 2) DIVIDED BY 26

GIVEN `wages in the highest quarter` IS A NUMBER, `wages in the second-highest quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly benefit amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount derived` `wages in the highest quarter` `wages in the second-highest quarter` AT MOST 44.5
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the amount derived` `wages in the highest quarter` `wages in the second-highest quarter` GREATER THAN 274.5
         THEN 275
         ELSE `to the dollar` (`the amount derived` `wages in the highest quarter` `wages in the second-highest quarter`)

§§ `s 25-4-77(a)(6) -- the base-period wage test`

-- Base-period wages "equal to or exceeding one and one-half times" the highest quarter, "and in addition, qualifies for
-- benefits under the provisions of Section 25-4-72" (a weekly benefit amount exists). Proviso: a person who received
-- benefits in the preceding benefit year must since have earned in insured work "at least eight times the weekly benefit
-- amount established for the individual in the preceding benefit year".
DECLARE `Base period` HAS
    `wages in the highest quarter`                       IS A NUMBER
    `wages in the second-highest quarter`                IS A NUMBER
    `total base-period wages`                            IS A NUMBER
    `received benefits in the preceding benefit year`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly benefit amount in the preceding benefit year` IS A NUMBER
    `insured wages earned since that benefit year began` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN b IS A `Base period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the base-period wage test` IF
        b's `total base-period wages` AT LEAST (1.5 TIMES b's `wages in the highest quarter`)
    AND `the weekly benefit amount` (b's `wages in the highest quarter`) (b's `wages in the second-highest quarter`) GREATER THAN 0
    AND (    NOT (b's `received benefits in the preceding benefit year`)
         OR  b's `insured wages earned since that benefit year began` AT LEAST (8 TIMES b's `weekly benefit amount in the preceding benefit year`))

§§ `s 25-4-74(a) -- the maximum total in a benefit year`

-- "the lesser of 14 times his or her weekly benefit amount, if the state's average unemployment rate is at or below 6.5
-- percent, with an additional weekly benefit amount added for each 0.5 percent increase ... above 6.5 percent up to a
-- maximum of 20 times ... if the state's average unemployment rate equals or exceeds 9.5 percent, and one fourth of the
-- wages paid ... during his or her base period". The rate is the one the Department of Workforce publishes ((d)): an input.
GIVEN `the state's average unemployment rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of weekly amounts` MEANS
    IF `the state's average unemployment rate` AT MOST 6.5
    THEN 14
    ELSE min 20 (14 PLUS FLOOR ((`the state's average unemployment rate` MINUS 6.5) DIVIDED BY 0.5))

GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER, `total base-period wages` IS A NUMBER, `the state's average unemployment rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total benefits` MEANS
    `to the dollar` (min (`the number of weekly amounts` `the state's average unemployment rate` TIMES `weekly benefit amount`)
                         (`total base-period wages` DIVIDED BY 4))

§§ `s 25-4-73 -- the payment for a week`

-- (a): "his or her weekly benefit amount, less that part of the wages, if any, payable to him or her with respect to such
-- week which is in excess of one third of the weekly benefit amount", to the nearest dollar. Never below nil.
GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER, `wages for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment for the week` MEANS
    max 0 (`to the dollar` (`weekly benefit amount` MINUS max 0 (`wages for the week` MINUS (`weekly benefit amount` DIVIDED BY 3))))

-- (c): "a one-week waiting period with no benefits payable during the first compensable week within a benefit year".
GIVEN `the first compensable week of the benefit year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a waiting week` IF `the first compensable week of the benefit year`

§§ `s 25-4-77(a)(1)-(5) -- eligibility for a week`

DECLARE `Week claimed` HAS
    `claim made for the week`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered and reporting at the employment office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `able to work and available for work`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `in approved training`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `totally or partially unemployed in the week`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `prospective employers contacted in the week`     IS A NUMBER
    `summoned for jury duty`                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a)(5): "contacting at least three prospective employers for each week of unemployment claimed", unless the failure is
-- because of a jury summons. (b)(1)-(2): approved training is no ground for denial under (a)(3).
GIVEN w IS A `Week claimed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `made a reasonable and active effort to secure work` IF
        w's `prospective employers contacted in the week` AT LEAST 3
    OR  w's `summoned for jury duty`

GIVEN w IS A `Week claimed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for the week` IF
        w's `claim made for the week`
    AND w's `registered and reporting at the employment office`
    AND (w's `able to work and available for work` OR w's `in approved training`)
    AND w's `totally or partially unemployed in the week`
    AND `made a reasonable and active effort to secure work` w

§§ `s 25-4-78 -- disqualifications for how the job ended`

-- How the worker's most recent bona fide work ended, in the categories s 25-4-78(2) and (3) use. Whether a quit had
-- "good cause connected with such work", and which kind of misconduct it was, are for the secretary; asked as facts.
DECLARE `How the job ended` IS ONE OF
    `laid off or let go for no fault of mine`
    `quit with good cause connected with the work`
    `quit without good cause connected with the work`
    -- (3)a: "a dishonest or criminal act committed in connection with his or her work or for sabotage or an act
    -- endangering the safety of others or for the use of illegal drugs after previous warning or for the refusal to
    -- submit to or cooperate with a blood or urine test after previous warning"
    `discharged for a dishonest or criminal act, sabotage, endangering others, or drugs after warning`
    -- (3)b: "actual or threatened misconduct ... repeated after previous warning"
    `discharged for misconduct repeated after warning`
    -- (3)c: "misconduct connected with his or her work" of any other kind
    `discharged for other misconduct connected with the work`

-- (2)a.1, c, d: a quit is not disqualifying where the worker was forced to leave by sickness or disability and met the
-- notice and return conditions, immediately returned to the regular employer or to recall rights, or relocated with an
-- active-duty military spouse. Asked as one fact.
DECLARE `Effect of the separation` IS ONE OF
    `no disqualification`
    -- (2)b, (3)b: no benefits "until" re-employment with wages of at least 10 times the weekly benefit amount and a
    -- nondisqualifying separation; the total reduced by 3 to 9 times the weekly benefit amount, as the secretary decides
    `no benefits until requalified, and the total reduced by 3 to 9 weekly amounts`
    -- (3)a: the same requalification, and never any benefits on the wages from that employer
    `no benefits until requalified, and none ever on that employer's wages`
    -- (3)c: the week of discharge and 1 to 4 following weeks, as the secretary decides; the total reduced by those weeks
    `no benefits for the week of discharge and 1 to 4 more weeks, and the total reduced by those weeks`

GIVEN `how` IS A `How the job ended`, `a quit exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of the separation`
`the effect of the separation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `laid off or let go for no fault of mine`         THEN `no disqualification`
    WHEN `quit with good cause connected with the work`    THEN `no disqualification`
    WHEN `quit without good cause connected with the work` THEN
        IF `a quit exception applies`
        THEN `no disqualification`
        ELSE `no benefits until requalified, and the total reduced by 3 to 9 weekly amounts`
    WHEN `discharged for a dishonest or criminal act, sabotage, endangering others, or drugs after warning` THEN `no benefits until requalified, and none ever on that employer's wages`
    WHEN `discharged for misconduct repeated after warning` THEN `no benefits until requalified, and the total reduced by 3 to 9 weekly amounts`
    WHEN `discharged for other misconduct connected with the work` THEN `no benefits for the week of discharge and 1 to 4 more weeks, and the total reduced by those weeks`

-- (2)b.1(ii), (3)a.1: requalifying needs insured wages "equal to at least 10 times his or her weekly benefit amount".
GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wages needed to requalify` MEANS 10 TIMES `weekly benefit amount`

-- (2)b.2, (3)c.2: the total of s 25-4-74 reduced by the number of weekly amounts the secretary sets.
GIVEN `maximum total` IS A NUMBER, `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER, `weekly amounts deducted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduced maximum total` MEANS
    max 0 (`maximum total` MINUS (`weekly amounts deducted` TIMES `weekly benefit amount`))

-- (5): failing without good cause to apply for or accept available suitable work: "not less than one nor more than five
-- weeks from the date of failure". (5)b: work is never suitable if the post is vacant because of a labour dispute, if its
-- wages, hours or conditions are substantially less favourable than prevailing locally, or if it requires joining a
-- company union or leaving a bona fide union.
GIVEN `vacant because of a strike, lockout or labor dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantially less favorable than prevailing local conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requires joining a company union or leaving a union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work can never be suitable` IF
        `vacant because of a strike, lockout or labor dispute`
    OR  `substantially less favorable than prevailing local conditions`
    OR  `requires joining a company union or leaving a union`

-- (8)b, c: the weekly benefit is reduced, not below nil, by a pension "reasonably attributable to the week" only if it is
-- paid under a plan maintained or contributed to by a base-period employer, 100 percent employer-financed; Social Security
-- and Railroad Retirement payments never reduce it. (8)b.2 (base-period work affecting the pension) is folded into the
-- first fact.
GIVEN `weekly payment` IS A NUMBER, `pension for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `paid under a base-period employer's plan, wholly employer-financed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Social Security or Railroad Retirement payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment after a pension` MEANS
    IF `paid under a base-period employer's plan, wholly employer-financed` AND (NOT `a Social Security or Railroad Retirement payment`)
    THEN max 0 (`weekly payment` MINUS `pension for the week`)
    ELSE `weekly payment`

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `the claimant's last employing unit`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `certify the week's work search` HAS `employers contacted` IS A NUMBER
    `file an appeal from the determination`
    `repay the disputed benefits to the fund`

-- s 25-4-77(a)(5): the claimant must contact "at least three prospective employers for each week of unemployment
-- claimed", and "The department shall require the claimant to provide proof of work search efforts when filing his or her
-- weekly certification". Modelled as the weekly certification, which counts only if it shows three or more employers
-- contacted. Days count from the start of the week claimed; the certification is taken to fall within the week (the
-- deadline for filing it is set by the secretary's rules, s 25-4-90, not deposited).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the weekly work search` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `certify the week's work search` `employers contacted` PROVIDED `employers contacted` AT LEAST 3
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `who` BECAUSE "s 25-4-77(a)(5): fewer than three prospective employers contacted; not eligible for the week"

-- s 25-4-91(d)(1): a party to whom notice of determination is given may appeal "within seven calendar days after delivery
-- of such notice or within 15 calendar days after such notice was mailed"; otherwise "such decision shall be deemed final".
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`, `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the right to appeal` `who` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MAY   `file an appeal from the determination`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED

GIVEN `the notice was mailed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days to appeal` MEANS
    IF `the notice was mailed`
    THEN 15
    ELSE 7

-- s 25-4-91(d)(1)a: if an appeal is filed, benefits paid before the final decision that "would not have been payable under
-- the terms of the final decision" are an overpayment, and "the claimant shall be required to repay". No time is stated.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to repay disputed benefits` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `repay the disputed benefits to the fund`

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the unemployed worker`
-- The seat: the individual who has lost work and claims benefits (the claimant). Each question is derived from the rules
-- above.

§§ `How much would I get?`

@export What is my Alabama weekly unemployment benefit amount (Ala. Code s 25-4-72)? 0 means no weekly benefit amount.
GIVEN `benefit year starts in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year your benefit year begins (the year you first claim)
      `my highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages for insured work in the calendar quarter of your base period with the most wages, in US dollars
      `my second-highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages for insured work in the quarter of your base period with the next most wages, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`What is my weekly benefit amount` MEANS
    IF `benefit year starts in` LESS THAN 2020
    THEN `not covered` `this encoding computes benefits for benefit years beginning on or after 1 January 2020 only`
    ELSE `answered` (`the weekly benefit amount` `my highest quarter wages` `my second-highest quarter wages`)

@export Have I earned enough in my base period to get Alabama unemployment benefits (Ala. Code s 25-4-77(a)(6))?
GIVEN `my highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages for insured work in the calendar quarter of your base period with the most wages, in US dollars
      `my second-highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages for insured work in the quarter of your base period with the next most wages, in US dollars
      `my total base-period wages` IS A NUMBER @desc All your wages for insured work in the four quarters of your base period, in US dollars
      `I got benefits last benefit year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive unemployment benefits in your preceding benefit year?
      `my last weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount in that preceding benefit year (0 if none)
      `my insured wages since then` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages you have earned in insured work since that preceding benefit year began, in US dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Have I earned enough to qualify` MEANS
    `meets the base-period wage test` (`Base period` WITH
        `wages in the highest quarter`                        IS `my highest quarter wages`
        `wages in the second-highest quarter`                 IS `my second-highest quarter wages`
        `total base-period wages`                             IS `my total base-period wages`
        `received benefits in the preceding benefit year`     IS `I got benefits last benefit year`
        `weekly benefit amount in the preceding benefit year` IS `my last weekly benefit amount`
        `insured wages earned since that benefit year began`  IS `my insured wages since then`)

@export What is the most Alabama unemployment benefit I can get in my benefit year (Ala. Code s 25-4-74(a))?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount, in US dollars
      `my total base-period wages` IS A NUMBER @desc All your wages for insured work in your base period, in US dollars
      `the state's unemployment rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The state's average unemployment rate published by the Alabama Department of Workforce for the most recent third calendar quarter, in percent (e.g. 3.1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can get in my benefit year` MEANS
    `the maximum total benefits` `my weekly benefit amount` `my total base-period wages` `the state's unemployment rate`

@export How much Alabama unemployment benefit will I be paid for a week in which I earned some wages (Ala. Code s 25-4-73(a))?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount, in US dollars
      `my wages this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages payable to you for the week, in US dollars (0 if none)
      `this is my first compensable week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first week of your benefit year for which you would otherwise be paid (the waiting week)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will I be paid for this week` MEANS
    IF `a waiting week` `this is my first compensable week`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the payment for the week` `my weekly benefit amount` `my wages this week`

§§ `Am I eligible this week?`

@export Am I eligible for Alabama unemployment benefits for this week (Ala. Code s 25-4-77(a)(1)-(5))?
GIVEN `I filed my claim for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file your weekly claim (certification) for the week?
      `I am registered and reporting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you registered for work and reporting at a state employment office as required?
      `I am able and available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you physically and mentally able to work, and available for work?
      `I am in approved training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a training course approved by the secretary, or Trade Act training?
      `I was unemployed this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you totally or partially unemployed this week?
      `employers I contacted this week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many different prospective employers did you contact this week?
      `I was summoned for jury duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a jury summons keep you from looking for work this week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I eligible this week` MEANS
    `eligible for the week` (`Week claimed` WITH
        `claim made for the week`                           IS `I filed my claim for the week`
        `registered and reporting at the employment office` IS `I am registered and reporting`
        `able to work and available for work`               IS `I am able and available`
        `in approved training`                              IS `I am in approved training`
        `totally or partially unemployed in the week`       IS `I was unemployed this week`
        `prospective employers contacted in the week`       IS `employers I contacted this week`
        `summoned for jury duty`                            IS `I was summoned for jury duty`)

§§ `How my job ended`

@export Does the way my last job ended disqualify me from Alabama unemployment benefits, and how (Ala. Code s 25-4-78(2), (3))?
GIVEN `how my job ended` IS A `How the job ended` @desc How your most recent job ended: laid off or let go for no fault of mine; quit with good cause connected with the work; quit without good cause connected with the work; discharged for a dishonest or criminal act, sabotage, endangering others, or drugs after warning; discharged for misconduct repeated after warning; discharged for other misconduct connected with the work
      `a quit exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you quit: were you forced out by sickness or disability (having told the employer and offered to return), did you go straight back to your regular employer or a job with recall rights, or did you move with an active-duty military spouse under orders?
GIVETH AN `Effect of the separation`
`Does how my job ended disqualify me` MEANS
    `the effect of the separation` `how my job ended` `a quit exception applies`

@export How much must I earn in a new insured job to requalify after a disqualification (Ala. Code s 25-4-78(2)b, (3)a)?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount for the benefit year of the disqualification, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I earn to requalify` MEANS
    `the wages needed to requalify` `my weekly benefit amount`

@export What is the most I can get in my benefit year after the secretary deducts weekly amounts for a disqualification (Ala. Code s 25-4-78(2)b.2, (3)c.2)?
GIVEN `my maximum total` IS A NUMBER @desc Your maximum total benefits for the benefit year before the reduction, in US dollars
      `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount, in US dollars
      `weekly amounts deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weekly amounts the secretary deducted (3 to 9 for a quit or repeated misconduct; the weeks of disqualification for other misconduct)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my reduced maximum` MEANS
    `the reduced maximum total` `my maximum total` `my weekly benefit amount` `weekly amounts deducted`

@export Can I refuse an offer of work without being disqualified because the work can never count as suitable (Ala. Code s 25-4-78(5)b)?
GIVEN `the job is vacant because of a strike` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the position vacant directly because of a strike, lockout or other labor dispute?
      `the job is worse than local conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its wages, hours or other conditions substantially less favorable than those prevailing for similar work locally?
      `the job requires a company union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have to join a company union, or resign from or not join a bona fide labor union?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I refuse this work` MEANS
    `the work can never be suitable` `the job is vacant because of a strike` `the job is worse than local conditions` `the job requires a company union`

@export How much is my weekly Alabama unemployment payment after a pension is taken off (Ala. Code s 25-4-78(8))?
GIVEN `my weekly payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit payment before the pension, in US dollars
      `my pension for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of your pension, retirement pay or annuity reasonably attributable to the week, in US dollars
      `the pension is from a base-period employer's plan it alone paid for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a plan of an employer you worked for in your base period, wholly financed by that employer?
      `the pension is Social Security or Railroad Retirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Social Security or Railroad Retirement payment?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my payment after my pension` MEANS
    `the payment after a pension` `my weekly payment` `my pension for the week` `the pension is from a base-period employer's plan it alone paid for` `the pension is Social Security or Railroad Retirement`

§§ `If I disagree with a decision`

@export How many days do I have to appeal an Alabama unemployment determination (Ala. Code s 25-4-91(d)(1))?
GIVEN `the notice was mailed to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of determination mailed to you (rather than delivered to you)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days do I have to appeal` MEANS
    `the days to appeal` `the notice was mailed to me`
